# Prompt Change Control Policy

## Never edit approved prompts
Once a prompt version has `approval_status: approved`, it is immutable.
Create a new version file instead.

```yaml
# ✅ GOOD — create a new version
prompts/versions/system-v1.2.0.md          # new file
prompts/versions/system-v1.2.0.proposal.yaml

# ❌ BAD — editing an approved version
# Do not edit system-v1.1.0.md if it has approval_status: approved
```

## Every proposal needs a rationale
"Better wording" is not a rationale. Describe the specific behavioral change and why it's needed.

## Update the registry
After approval, update `prompts/registry.yaml` to reflect the new active version and mark the old one as `superseded`.

## Breaking changes bump major
If a prompt change could cause an agent to behave differently in a way that breaks downstream systems, it's a major version bump.
